Final intuition
This experiment is asking whether MDMs have a real advantage over AR models:

Can they use scattered known tokens to infer the whole sequence globally?

If yes, then decoding should not just be “pick the most confident next token.” It should actively choose anchors that maximize global information gain. That would make MDM decoding more like building a scaffold first, then filling in the gaps.


